T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Derive the Norton Equivalent Circuit for a DC source of 30V having an internal) Tj
T*
(resistance of 5 Omega connected to a parallel branch of 10 Omega. Determine the current) Tj
T*
(delivered to a 15 Omega load resistor connected across the output terminals.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate Norton Short-Circuit Current I_N:) Tj
T*
(Short-circuit the load terminals. The 10 Omega resistor is bypassed by the short) Tj
T*
(circuit.) Tj
T*
(The short-circuit current is limited only by the 5 Omega resistor:) Tj
T*
(I_sc = I_N = V / R_internal = 30 V / 5 Omega = 6.0 Amperes.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Norton Resistance R_N:) Tj
T*
(Deactivate 30V source to short circuit. Looking into output terminals:) Tj
T*
(R_N = 5 Omega in parallel with 10 Omega = \(5 * 10\) / \(5 + 10\) = 50 / 15 = 3.33 Omega) Tj
T*
